1
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:12,233
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:40,767
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:43,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:46,467
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,767
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:59,600
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:00,667
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:02,333
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:04,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:07,267
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:11,467
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:17,333
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:19,300
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:22,233
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,233 --> 00:01:25,000
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:28,433
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:31,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:33,367 --> 00:01:34,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,167 --> 00:01:36,500
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:37,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,733 --> 00:01:39,033
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:41,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,667
<i>- Gabo!
- Tatang?</i>

24
00:01:47,667 --> 00:01:49,667
<i> Out here, we don't call him
Tatang.</i>

25
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:51,400
<i>- We call him Papang.
- How did you get out of jail?</i>

26
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,600
<i> Let me explain everything.</i>

27
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:56,367
<i> We went to the jewelry stores
in Chinatown.</i>

28
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:57,533
<i> All of the stores there</i>

29
00:01:57,533 --> 00:02:00,067
<i>are owned by a man
named Mr. Chan.</i>

30
00:02:00,067 --> 00:02:01,367
<i> I want a printed report.</i>

31
00:02:01,367 --> 00:02:03,100
<i> I need some information
about Mr. Chan.</i>

32
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:05,167
<i> We shouldn't make a mistake
on our report later.</i>

33
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:06,567
<i>Someone will be sitting
on our briefing.</i>

34
00:02:06,567 --> 00:02:08,100
<i>- Who?
- Hi, guys!</i>

35
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,667
[CLEARS THROAT] Are you ready?

36
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:13,200
<i> The chaos around is rampant.</i>

37
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,333
<i> Even our government</i>

38
00:02:14,367 --> 00:02:16,700
<i>can't contain the surge
of criminals anymore.</i>

39
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:20,200
<i> We need someone
who is wholehearted.</i>

40
00:02:20,567 --> 00:02:22,467
<i> A good fighter,</i>

41
00:02:22,467 --> 00:02:25,733
<i> fearless, and someone
with integrity.</i>

42
00:02:25,733 --> 00:02:28,200
<i> We need you, Gabo.</i>

43
00:02:28,567 --> 00:02:29,733
<i> Gabo, Anino needs you</i>

44
00:02:29,733 --> 00:02:32,800
<i> to act as their hands
in taking down criminals.</i>

45
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,200
<i>Gabo, Anino pays well
for every mission you complete.</i>

46
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,433
Macaraig almost beat me to death
<i> back inside that prison.</i>

47
00:02:38,433 --> 00:02:40,233
<i>Turns out he was just
playing me.</i>

48
00:02:40,233 --> 00:02:41,600
<i> Yeah, I need cash.</i>

49
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,333
<i> But not like this.</i>

50
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:46,100
<i> Hold on. Leave us alone
for a moment.</i>

51
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,600
- [DOOR OPENS]
- [SALVADOR GRUNTS]

52
00:02:48,233 --> 00:02:50,767
- [SALVADOR SIGHS HEAVILY]
- [DOOR CREAKS CLOSE]

53
00:02:50,767 --> 00:02:52,467
Oh, man.

54
00:02:52,467 --> 00:02:56,600
How are we gonna make
that controversial report?

55
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,167
You're so dense, Salvador.

56
00:02:59,167 --> 00:03:01,333
Boss Arnel made himself
very clear!

57
00:03:01,333 --> 00:03:03,800
If no one's paying attention,
then get their attention!

58
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,267
Clickbait reporting!

59
00:03:05,267 --> 00:03:06,733
Shut up, Oli.

60
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,733
You don't have the guts
to do that anyway.

61
00:03:10,667 --> 00:03:11,633
[SIGHS]

62
00:03:11,633 --> 00:03:13,633
You know... [THUDS]

63
00:03:13,633 --> 00:03:16,400
Just do whatever
Boss Arnel says

64
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:18,767
if you don't want
to lose your job.

65
00:03:18,767 --> 00:03:20,167
Obviously.

66
00:03:20,167 --> 00:03:21,267
Let's go.

67
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:23,933
Let's look for someone
who knows about this case.

68
00:03:23,933 --> 00:03:25,433
Wait, wait, wait.

69
00:03:26,967 --> 00:03:28,633
Our mindset...

70
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:29,933
has to be high.

71
00:03:29,933 --> 00:03:31,500
The higher the energy,

72
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,667
the higher the ratings.

73
00:03:34,267 --> 00:03:35,300
That's right.

74
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,200
Let's go. You got this!

75
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,033
[DOOR CLOSES]

76
00:03:38,033 --> 00:03:40,600
[GABO BREATHES SHAKILY]
Tatang...

77
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,800
I want to change.

78
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,567
This work will change
everything,

79
00:03:46,533 --> 00:03:48,167
for you,

80
00:03:48,433 --> 00:03:51,633
and it'll lift up
your whole family too.

81
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:56,433
One hundred thousand
per mission, Gabo.

82
00:03:56,700 --> 00:04:02,533
One hundred thousand pesos
to join Anino fully.

83
00:04:03,533 --> 00:04:04,633
[INHALES SHARPLY]

84
00:04:04,633 --> 00:04:06,000
Let me think about it.

85
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:12,933
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,300
[DOOR OPENS]

87
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:32,000
[ALARM BEEPING]

88
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:38,433
- [DIGITAL TRILL]
- [BEEPING CONTINUES]

89
00:04:38,433 --> 00:04:42,833
[GATE CREAKING OPEN]

90
00:04:42,833 --> 00:04:49,367
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

91
00:04:49,367 --> 00:04:51,000
[GATE CLOSES]

92
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,900
[BEEPING CONTINUES]

93
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,200
[DIGITAL TRILL]

94
00:05:03,767 --> 00:05:05,700
[VAN ENGINE REVVS]

95
00:05:06,533 --> 00:05:07,300
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

96
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:09,567
- Open it up already.
- Got it.

97
00:05:09,567 --> 00:05:10,533
[VAN DOOR CLOSES]
There they are, the cops.

98
00:05:10,533 --> 00:05:11,933
- Roll the camera now.
- Hey, you ready?

99
00:05:11,933 --> 00:05:13,267
That bald guy right there.

100
00:05:13,267 --> 00:05:15,700
He's the one who pushed
me around, real tough act.

101
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:19,900
Hey! What's this?
Why are you here?

102
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:20,933
We're just following up

103
00:05:20,933 --> 00:05:24,567
regarding the demolition
out at Ginintuang Lupa.

104
00:05:24,567 --> 00:05:26,400
- Sir, don't try anything.
- You need to leave.

105
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,900
Nobody here's
going to talk to you.

106
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:30,900
You won't speak up

107
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:34,967
because you don't want what
you've been doing there exposed.

108
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,767
That's police brutality, man.
You're trigger-happy, bro.

109
00:05:38,767 --> 00:05:40,733
Hold on, what exactly is
going on here right now?

110
00:05:40,733 --> 00:05:43,333
What do you mean
police brutality?

111
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:44,933
We're simply enforcing the law.

112
00:05:44,933 --> 00:05:47,433
You saw yourselves,
we have a court order

113
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:49,900
for that demolition operation.

114
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,800
What are you doing here anyway?

115
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,833
Just looking to pick
a fight or start trouble?

116
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:57,567
We're here to find out
the truth.

117
00:05:57,567 --> 00:06:01,300
Alright,
if you want your side heard...

118
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:04,500
what's your commanding officer's
name? Call him out here.

119
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:07,300
Santos, get the Colonel.

120
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,433
Let him see exactly
what this guy's looking for.

121
00:06:09,467 --> 00:06:12,467
- Go on.
- Now you're making threats?

122
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:13,800
- Fine.
- Just one moment.

123
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,900
- We'll get him.
- Yeah, sure thing.

124
00:06:18,633 --> 00:06:22,433
Sir, that reporter from
the demolition site is here.

125
00:06:22,433 --> 00:06:24,800
- He needs to speak with you.
- [SCOFFS]

126
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:27,467
They're really pushing it.

127
00:06:27,467 --> 00:06:29,100
Is that so?
[GLASS THUDS]

128
00:06:30,767 --> 00:06:35,433
Fine, let's see just how far
this guy's nerve will take him.

129
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:39,767
- Let's go meet them.
- He's here.

130
00:06:39,767 --> 00:06:41,667
Colonel,
they're from Manila Telebalita.

131
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,033
Good evening, Colonel.

132
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,500
Put that down.
They're going to talk.

133
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:47,667
- What are you doing?
- I said--

134
00:06:47,667 --> 00:06:49,900
I've already seen your report.

135
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:51,667
You're Salvador, right?

136
00:06:51,667 --> 00:06:53,167
That's correct, Colonel.

137
00:06:53,167 --> 00:06:55,967
Why did your operation
turn so violent?

138
00:06:55,967 --> 00:06:58,733
Your men went too far,
that's brutality.

139
00:06:58,733 --> 00:07:00,067
Your men are trigger-happy.

140
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:01,900
That's not true.

141
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,467
- We operated with...
- Quit it.

142
00:07:03,467 --> 00:07:05,033
...maximum tolerance
every step of the way.

143
00:07:05,333 --> 00:07:07,067
People from Ginintuang Lupa

144
00:07:07,067 --> 00:07:09,233
were the ones who started
using force and aggression.

145
00:07:09,233 --> 00:07:13,867
Maximum tolerance?
Someone got shot! People hurt!

146
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,933
That's police brutality,
Colonel!

147
00:07:15,933 --> 00:07:19,767
That area was a hotbed for
every kind of criminal activity.

148
00:07:19,767 --> 00:07:23,733
All sorts of weapons were
scattered all over that place.

149
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:26,200
Just admit
what you've been doing!

150
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,933
This is too much!
Total abuse of power!

151
00:07:27,933 --> 00:07:29,833
- You just don't stop, do you?!
- What do you mean?!

152
00:07:29,833 --> 00:07:33,100
We maintain peace and order,
that's our job!

153
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:35,100
I saw everything
with my own two eyes!

154
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:37,933
- Are you accusing--
- That was police brutality!

155
00:07:37,933 --> 00:07:39,767
- Are you accusing me?!
- Yes!

156
00:07:39,767 --> 00:07:41,033
- Lies!
- It's the truth!

157
00:07:41,033 --> 00:07:43,367
Watch your words
very carefully, you hear?!

158
00:07:43,367 --> 00:07:45,667
I know exactly
why you showed up here.

159
00:07:45,667 --> 00:07:47,867
You want our official statement,

160
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:50,467
then twist it all around,
drag our name through mud,

161
00:07:50,467 --> 00:07:52,400
and blow this whole thing
out of proportion.

162
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:55,233
That's exactly
how the media operates!

163
00:07:55,233 --> 00:07:56,800
I'm only here
to uncover the facts!

164
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,300
- You want the truth?!
- Yes!

165
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:01,200
There was no police
brutality whatsoever!

166
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,733
- That's enough, Colonel!
- What did you say?!

167
00:08:02,733 --> 00:08:04,800
I'm going to expose
everything you've done!

168
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,300
You bastard!
Let go of me!

169
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,233
- Colonel!
- Calm down, sir.

170
00:08:08,233 --> 00:08:09,767
That's enough. Easy now, sir.

171
00:08:09,767 --> 00:08:11,900
- Go! Get him out of here!
- Come on.

172
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:16,200
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,400
Let's go, Colonel.

174
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:23,833
[OLI] Seriously, Salvador.

175
00:08:23,833 --> 00:08:25,600
You surprised me there, man.

176
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,267
You were so brave!

177
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:29,700
That's exactly
what Boss Arnel wants.

178
00:08:30,267 --> 00:08:34,067
It's a shame I couldn't take
a video of it!

179
00:08:34,267 --> 00:08:36,767
I'm sure the
boss will be pleased.

180
00:08:36,767 --> 00:08:38,567
- Conversation?
- Yes.

181
00:08:38,567 --> 00:08:40,800
That was a brawl.
I almost got in trouble,

182
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:42,733
and you're worried
you didn't record it?

183
00:08:42,733 --> 00:08:45,333
Well, what can I do?
They don't want to.

184
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:47,100
At least I put
in my best effort.

185
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:50,100
We can't come empty-handed
to Boss Arnel.

186
00:08:51,567 --> 00:08:53,067
Here's what we'll do.

187
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:56,400
If we didn't get anything
from whoever fired the gun,

188
00:08:56,433 --> 00:08:57,833
let's just make up
a story instead.

189
00:08:58,433 --> 00:08:59,800
Say it was a stray bullet.

190
00:09:01,133 --> 00:09:02,600
[NEIL] That's insane!

191
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,533
Just because of
a few rotten cops,

192
00:09:04,533 --> 00:09:06,633
it's so easy for them to make it
look like all of us are bad.

193
00:09:07,267 --> 00:09:09,300
We're just doing our job!

194
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,733
We are just following the law.

195
00:09:11,333 --> 00:09:13,167
And then we're the ones
who get blamed?

196
00:09:13,167 --> 00:09:14,433
We'll even get criticized.

197
00:09:16,133 --> 00:09:17,233
[SIGHS]

198
00:09:18,167 --> 00:09:19,333
[THUDS]

199
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,700
Well, you can't blame them.

200
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:24,400
There really are many
in our ranks who are rotten

201
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:27,300
and abusive of their power.

202
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,567
It's like a pile of tomatoes.

203
00:09:30,567 --> 00:09:32,167
If you mix one rotten one,

204
00:09:32,567 --> 00:09:33,733
they all start to rot.

205
00:09:33,733 --> 00:09:35,300
That's why we

206
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:37,900
should continue being good cops.

207
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:39,467
To prove to the people

208
00:09:39,467 --> 00:09:41,300
that there are good cops.

209
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:43,433
Let's just stick
to what is right, okay?

210
00:09:44,367 --> 00:09:45,267
Yes, ma'am.

211
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:51,167
Maybe we can
find something here.

212
00:09:51,167 --> 00:09:52,933
Maybe the victim's
family is here.

213
00:09:53,467 --> 00:09:54,667
Miss?

214
00:09:54,667 --> 00:09:57,800
Uh, we're from Telebalita.

215
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,533
They say the victims

216
00:09:59,533 --> 00:10:01,700
of the demolition at Ginintuang
Lupa were brought here.

217
00:10:01,733 --> 00:10:02,700
Yes, sir.

218
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:04,533
Can we talk to
them?

219
00:10:04,533 --> 00:10:06,200
I'm afraid you can't.

220
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,567
He is in the ICU.

221
00:10:07,867 --> 00:10:09,900
But his family is here.

222
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:11,567
[SALVADR] Alright,
we'll talk to them.

223
00:10:11,567 --> 00:10:12,633
Thank you.

224
00:10:14,233 --> 00:10:16,367
I think this
is the victim's family.

225
00:10:16,767 --> 00:10:17,867
Ma'am?

226
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:19,900
Good evening.

227
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:22,567
I'm Salvador Manalo.

228
00:10:22,567 --> 00:10:24,000
We work for Manila Telebalita.

229
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,667
We're covering

230
00:10:25,667 --> 00:10:28,700
the demolition that happened
in Ginintuang Lupa.

231
00:10:29,733 --> 00:10:30,733
Do you live there?

232
00:10:30,933 --> 00:10:32,400
Yes, we live there.

233
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,467
Are you the family
of the person who was shot?

234
00:10:34,867 --> 00:10:37,433
[MAMENG] Ah, he's my husband.

235
00:10:37,433 --> 00:10:38,767
I'm the sister of the person
who got shot.

236
00:10:38,767 --> 00:10:41,633
She's the wife of the person
who was shot.

237
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:43,367
This a big story.

238
00:10:43,367 --> 00:10:45,367
The public needs
to know about this.

239
00:10:45,367 --> 00:10:46,700
So...

240
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:48,333
may I interview you?

241
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:49,833
Yes, you can.

242
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:52,900
So they can know
what really happened.

243
00:10:53,867 --> 00:10:56,367
Okay, ma'am.
Let's look for a spot.

244
00:10:56,367 --> 00:10:57,400
Let's go.

245
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,600
Here?

246
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:02,600
[OMENG] Pops.

247
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:04,833
Have you convinced him yet?

248
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,500
[TOMAS] Did Gabo agree?

249
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:11,700
Put him back in jail, pops.

250
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,500
He'll be useless, pops.

251
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:15,633
He's faint-hearted.

252
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:17,767
[LAWIN] What I don't
understand, pops,

253
00:11:17,767 --> 00:11:20,500
is why you're
so impressed with him.

254
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:21,467
[UWAK] He's right.

255
00:11:21,467 --> 00:11:24,467
Out of all our members,
he's the weakest.

256
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:26,767
Give it to them.

257
00:11:26,767 --> 00:11:33,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,300
[OMENG] You already know
what to do.

259
00:11:36,067 --> 00:11:37,267
Here.

260
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,967
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

261
00:11:48,967 --> 00:11:50,633
Hey, it's Gabo.

262
00:11:50,633 --> 00:11:52,600
[PRISCILLA] Gabo! Gabo!

263
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,933
How's your dad doing?

264
00:11:53,933 --> 00:12:00,900
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

265
00:12:03,433 --> 00:12:05,233
- His condition is not good.
- Gabo.

266
00:12:06,033 --> 00:12:07,267
Paquito is here.

267
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,933
He knows what you did to Django.

268
00:12:10,267 --> 00:12:11,467
Be careful.

269
00:12:13,767 --> 00:12:15,433
I don't care about them.

270
00:12:16,367 --> 00:12:17,933
Because when our paths
crossed,

271
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:20,667
I would knock them down.

272
00:12:20,667 --> 00:12:24,733
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:12:24,733 --> 00:12:27,000
- Why don't you come in?
- Come in!

274
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,633
- Come inside!
- C'mon!

275
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:31,000
I feel sorry for that kid.

276
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,033
He just got released,

277
00:12:32,033 --> 00:12:35,467
and now he's carrying
another huge problem.

278
00:12:35,467 --> 00:12:36,700
You're right.

279
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,833
His problems
never stopped coming

280
00:12:39,833 --> 00:12:41,967
ever since he was a child.

281
00:12:41,967 --> 00:12:43,667
He's had all kinds of bad luck.

282
00:12:43,667 --> 00:12:45,067
His mother died,

283
00:12:45,067 --> 00:12:47,133
and now his father
has been shot.

284
00:12:47,133 --> 00:12:51,800
And now,
Paquito is hunting him down.

285
00:12:51,833 --> 00:12:54,500
- You're right.
- I feel so bad for him.

286
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,167
Once he faces
Pacquito and Django,

287
00:12:56,167 --> 00:12:58,900
one of them
is surely going down.

288
00:12:59,833 --> 00:13:01,033
Yes, you're right.

289
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:03,900
- Ready.
- Yes.

290
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:06,000
Okay.
Okay, ma'am.

291
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,600
I witnessed the violence

292
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,833
and the abuse you suffered
at the hands of the police

293
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:14,333
during the demolition
at Ginintuang Lupa.

294
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:19,367
We are just fighting
for what is right.

295
00:13:19,833 --> 00:13:24,633
We have the right to stay
in Ginintuang Lupa.

296
00:13:24,933 --> 00:13:29,033
Then they just made us leave,
just like that.

297
00:13:29,033 --> 00:13:30,800
Like we were pests.

298
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:33,100
For everyone's information,

299
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:35,533
may I ask your relation to
Sir Rudy, the man who got shot?

300
00:13:35,533 --> 00:13:36,833
He's my husband.

301
00:13:37,067 --> 00:13:40,100
I'm Rudy Magtibay's wife.

302
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:41,833
Uh, how is he doing now?

303
00:13:43,967 --> 00:13:45,867
He's still in the ICU.

304
00:13:46,533 --> 00:13:48,433
He's still unconscious.

305
00:13:48,433 --> 00:13:50,833
He needs to undergo
a surgery but...

306
00:13:51,567 --> 00:13:53,367
we don't have money.

307
00:13:54,567 --> 00:13:55,800
[SOBBING SOFTLY]

308
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:58,067
My husband is a very kind man.

309
00:13:58,067 --> 00:14:01,067
I don't...
I don't understand

310
00:14:01,067 --> 00:14:03,567
why they did that to him.

311
00:14:03,567 --> 00:14:05,667
Is it because we are poor?

312
00:14:05,667 --> 00:14:08,967
Don't we have the
right to live?

313
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:11,900
To love? To dream?

314
00:14:13,067 --> 00:14:16,933
We were just trying to fight
for what was right.

315
00:14:16,933 --> 00:14:20,733
We know that Ginintuang Lupa
is rightfully ours.

316
00:14:22,067 --> 00:14:26,133
I won't be able to live
with myself if Rudy dies.

317
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,133
[BETCHAY SOBBING]

318
00:14:29,133 --> 00:14:32,067
What do you want to say
to our viewers?

319
00:14:35,767 --> 00:14:37,500
I'm...

320
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:40,000
I'm asking all of you...

321
00:14:40,533 --> 00:14:43,967
To those who have
a kind heart...

322
00:14:44,933 --> 00:14:49,733
we're here at
Torres Medical Center.

323
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:53,067
Rudy needs to undergo
an operation.

324
00:14:53,867 --> 00:14:58,267
If you can,
even if it's a small amount,

325
00:14:58,267 --> 00:15:00,900
please help us.

326
00:15:02,667 --> 00:15:04,233
I'm begging you.

327
00:15:04,233 --> 00:15:08,167
My husband has to live.

328
00:15:08,167 --> 00:15:09,200
[SNIFFLES]

329
00:15:10,633 --> 00:15:11,967
Uh... Well, then,

330
00:15:11,967 --> 00:15:13,633
let's wrap it up here.

331
00:15:13,633 --> 00:15:15,900
- Thank you very much.
- [BETCHAY] Yes.

332
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:17,967
Thank you. Thank you.

333
00:15:17,967 --> 00:15:19,633
- I'm sorry.
- Thank you.

334
00:15:20,967 --> 00:15:22,200
Thank you.

335
00:15:33,667 --> 00:15:35,233
[KEYS JINGLE]

336
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:36,700
- [LOCK CLICKS]
- [DOOR OPENS, CREAKS]

337
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:43,667
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:15:59,233 --> 00:16:01,033
[GABO] All this time,
I thought...

339
00:16:04,167 --> 00:16:05,567
<i> I was already free.</i>

340
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:08,967
<i> I didn't know
that my freedom...</i>

341
00:16:11,867 --> 00:16:13,100
<i> comes with a price.</i>

342
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:17,933
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

343
00:16:19,700 --> 00:16:26,067
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:16:27,533 --> 00:16:28,767
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

345
00:16:43,833 --> 00:16:51,367
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

346
00:16:54,433 --> 00:16:59,233
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

347
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:05,300
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

348
00:17:18,333 --> 00:17:19,333
[SWORD CLANKS]

349
00:17:35,867 --> 00:17:37,300
- [DOOR OPENS]
- [WOMAN GASPS]

350
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:49,600
- It's Gabo.
- Oh, what's Gabo holding?

351
00:17:49,633 --> 00:17:50,833
What's that on his hands?

352
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,667
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

353
00:18:07,533 --> 00:18:09,367
[PLASTIC RUSTLES]

354
00:18:18,733 --> 00:18:19,900
Who left this?

355
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:21,167
We don't know, Gabo.

356
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,067
Did you see anyone?

357
00:18:22,067 --> 00:18:23,367
- We didn't, Gabo.
- We didn't, Gabo.

358
00:18:23,367 --> 00:18:27,400
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

359
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:34,333
[MUSIC TURNS PENSIVE]

360
00:18:40,533 --> 00:18:41,533
[DOOR CLOSES]

361
00:18:41,533 --> 00:18:44,700
Our intel says we can catch
the syndicates

362
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:46,500
involved in gold smuggling case.

363
00:18:46,767 --> 00:18:48,200
It's Chinese New Year tomorrow.

364
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:49,667
Many will be in in Chinatown.

365
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:52,400
Our lead will be Mr. Chan.

366
00:18:53,167 --> 00:18:54,833
He's the known associate of...

367
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:56,833
Victor.

368
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:59,867
- Victor Zafra alias Tiger.
- Confirmed.

369
00:19:00,233 --> 00:19:04,100
Tomorrow, Mr. Chan will have
a transaction,

370
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:06,200
and it's likely
with Victor Zafra.

371
00:19:06,733 --> 00:19:08,467
Intentionally
on Chinese New Year.

372
00:19:08,467 --> 00:19:11,667
Now, we're not sure where
they'll do the transaction.

373
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,733
Or if they will really
meet up tomorrow.

374
00:19:13,733 --> 00:19:15,200
Chinatown is huge.

375
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:18,433
Does that mean
you'll be going in blind?

376
00:19:23,367 --> 00:19:24,367
No, ma'am.

377
00:19:24,633 --> 00:19:28,233
We know
where Mr. Chan frequents.

378
00:19:28,767 --> 00:19:29,767
A bar.

379
00:19:30,433 --> 00:19:31,567
Jade Imperial.

380
00:19:32,467 --> 00:19:33,533
There's a possibility.

381
00:19:34,233 --> 00:19:35,400
So that means...

382
00:19:36,767 --> 00:19:38,233
you're still not sure.

383
00:19:39,733 --> 00:19:41,367
Oh, so she expects intel
from a magic crystal ball.

384
00:19:41,767 --> 00:19:44,767
We may not know
what exactly happens tomorrow,

385
00:19:44,767 --> 00:19:46,533
but I can assure you one thing.

386
00:19:46,767 --> 00:19:48,767
The whole team knows what to do,

387
00:19:48,767 --> 00:19:50,400
no matter the situation.

388
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,900
There will be
an exclusive party at the bar.

389
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,600
That's the perfect cover
for the transaction.

390
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:59,867
Guys, this is our mission.

391
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,467
We have to keep Mr. Chan
under surveillance

392
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:05,300
from his jewelry store
until he leaves.

393
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:06,800
We will follow him anywhere

394
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:09,467
because he's our lead to where
the transaction will take place.

395
00:20:10,167 --> 00:20:11,733
Castor, Rallos,

396
00:20:12,533 --> 00:20:13,667
you'll be at the van.

397
00:20:13,867 --> 00:20:15,300
Keep an eye on the surroundings.

398
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:16,433
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

399
00:20:16,633 --> 00:20:17,800
[SEBASTIAN] Guys.

400
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:20,133
We need to catch Victor Zafra.

401
00:20:20,533 --> 00:20:22,300
This might be our only chance.

402
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:23,833
Let's keep our eyes peeled.

403
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:25,900
Tiger is a very large fish
to catch.

404
00:20:26,367 --> 00:20:27,500
We can't fail on this mission.

405
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:28,733
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

406
00:20:28,933 --> 00:20:31,467
I told you, she's prepared.

407
00:20:31,467 --> 00:20:38,433
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

408
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:52,467
[MUSIC FADES]

409
00:20:53,233 --> 00:21:00,200
- [ROUSING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [MEN HOLLERING]

410
00:21:07,467 --> 00:21:08,500
[BLOW LANDS]

411
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:11,300
[MEN CHEERING]

412
00:21:12,233 --> 00:21:13,367
[BLOWS LAND]

413
00:21:13,367 --> 00:21:14,300
[KICK LANDS]

414
00:21:16,567 --> 00:21:17,700
[KICKS LAND]

415
00:21:23,267 --> 00:21:24,233
[BLOW LANDS]

416
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:26,900
[KICK LANDS, BLOWS LAND]

417
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:29,467
[BLOW LANDS]

418
00:21:31,233 --> 00:21:33,333
[BLOWS LAND]

419
00:21:35,267 --> 00:21:36,833
[BLOWS LAND]

420
00:21:37,233 --> 00:21:38,500
[GRUNTING] Argh!

421
00:21:38,767 --> 00:21:39,733
[BODY THUDS]

422
00:21:40,367 --> 00:21:44,333
[BLOWS LAND]

423
00:21:46,267 --> 00:21:47,867
[BLOWS LAND]

424
00:21:47,867 --> 00:21:49,000
You bastard!

425
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:51,267
- [KICK LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

426
00:21:58,767 --> 00:22:00,000
[KICK LANDS, BLOW LANDS]

427
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,867
- [BLOW LANDS, KICK LANDS]
- [MAN GRUNTS]

428
00:22:05,567 --> 00:22:06,533
[BODY THUDS]

429
00:22:06,733 --> 00:22:08,500
[BLOWS LAND]

430
00:22:09,267 --> 00:22:10,433
[BLOWS LAND]

431
00:22:10,867 --> 00:22:12,767
- Hey, stop it!
- That's enough, boss!

432
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,267
[BLOW LANDS, KICKS LAND]

433
00:22:15,933 --> 00:22:17,767
- [KICKS LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

434
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:19,767
- [BLOW LANDS]
- You wuss!

435
00:22:20,833 --> 00:22:23,767
[MEN GRUNTING]

436
00:22:23,767 --> 00:22:25,733
That's what you get
for not respecting your boss!

437
00:22:25,733 --> 00:22:28,600
Victor! I knew
they were ganging up on me!

438
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,833
Boss, it's a sparring session.

439
00:22:30,833 --> 00:22:32,300
It's part of the training, boss.

440
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,367
You had the nerve
to talk back, huh?

441
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:37,400
[SWORD CLANKS]

442
00:22:38,933 --> 00:22:39,967
- [KICK LANDS]
- [MAN GRUNTS]

443
00:22:39,967 --> 00:22:41,100
- Boss! Boss!
- Boss! Boss!

444
00:22:41,100 --> 00:22:42,400
That's enough.

445
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,967
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

446
00:22:45,967 --> 00:22:47,033
Victor.

447
00:22:50,967 --> 00:22:52,333
[KICK LANDS, GRUNTS] Argh!

448
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
You okay?

449
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,100
I'm alright, Victor.

450
00:23:04,033 --> 00:23:06,067
Are you just going to kill
all of our men?

451
00:23:06,667 --> 00:23:09,933
Ma, I'm just reminding them
to know their place.

452
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,400
Wrap it up.

453
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:16,667
We'll talk inside.

454
00:23:17,633 --> 00:23:24,600
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

455
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:27,500
[DOUBLE DOOR OPENING]

456
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:34,333
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

457
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:46,200
What is this?

458
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:48,233
It's only worth
a hundred million.

459
00:23:48,233 --> 00:23:50,667
This is less than half
of the promised delivery.

460
00:23:50,667 --> 00:23:51,867
What happened?

461
00:23:51,867 --> 00:23:54,000
[ARTURO] Sir, according
to our workers in the refinery,

462
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,567
the equipment shut down,

463
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:57,000
which caused a delay
in production.

464
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,400
[DEBORAH] That's b*.

465
00:23:58,400 --> 00:24:01,567
They knew all too well that
people want those gold bars,

466
00:24:01,567 --> 00:24:03,767
so they had to be prepared.

467
00:24:03,767 --> 00:24:04,733
[CLICKS TONGUE]

468
00:24:04,733 --> 00:24:06,267
- Victor.
- Pa.

469
00:24:06,267 --> 00:24:07,867
Which client
will you supply first?

470
00:24:07,867 --> 00:24:09,767
I have a deal with Mr. Chan.

471
00:24:09,767 --> 00:24:11,900
We'll meet tomorrow
in Chinatown.

472
00:24:11,900 --> 00:24:12,733
[DEBORAH SCOFFS]

473
00:24:12,733 --> 00:24:15,067
[CHUCKLES DRYLY]
That's small-time!

474
00:24:15,067 --> 00:24:18,767
I know, Ma, but ninety percent
of that will go to Malaysia.

475
00:24:18,767 --> 00:24:19,933
After my meeting with Mr. Chan,

476
00:24:19,933 --> 00:24:21,833
we'll go to a port in Mindanao

477
00:24:21,833 --> 00:24:24,267
to smuggle them abroad.

478
00:24:24,267 --> 00:24:25,900
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

479
00:24:25,900 --> 00:24:28,267
I like the way you think.

480
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:29,367
Very good.

481
00:24:29,367 --> 00:24:30,333
[GENTLE TAPPING]

482
00:24:32,367 --> 00:24:33,400
Lucas,

483
00:24:33,933 --> 00:24:35,900
you should always
follow your brother

484
00:24:36,467 --> 00:24:39,467
so that you can learn how
to run our business.

485
00:24:39,467 --> 00:24:41,267
[DEBORAH] Lucas knows all that.

486
00:24:41,767 --> 00:24:43,567
He's been doing that
for a long time.

487
00:24:43,567 --> 00:24:44,967
You just have to trust him.

488
00:24:44,967 --> 00:24:47,067
We'll get there, darling.

489
00:24:47,067 --> 00:24:48,633
For now, though,

490
00:24:48,633 --> 00:24:51,100
Victor is going to take
care of everything.

491
00:24:51,100 --> 00:24:54,900
Lucas, don't ever leave
your brother's side.

492
00:24:54,900 --> 00:24:55,900
Okay?

493
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:57,767
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

494
00:24:57,767 --> 00:24:58,733
Yes, Papa.

495
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:07,400
[GLASS THUDS]

496
00:25:11,067 --> 00:25:12,633
[MUSIC FADES]

497
00:25:15,767 --> 00:25:20,467
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

498
00:25:20,467 --> 00:25:21,433
[SOFT THUD]

499
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:24,300
[BLADE SLIDES, CLICKS]

500
00:25:35,100 --> 00:25:42,067
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

501
00:25:57,033 --> 00:26:03,433
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

502
00:26:03,433 --> 00:26:04,933
- [BUTTON CLICKS]
- [TABLET CHIMES]

503
00:26:08,033 --> 00:26:09,000
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

504
00:26:09,033 --> 00:26:12,100
<i> If you're watching this video,</i>

505
00:26:13,033 --> 00:26:17,067
<i>it means you've accepted
the mission.</i>

506
00:26:17,067 --> 00:26:19,700
<i> In the first picture is a man</i>

507
00:26:19,700 --> 00:26:24,500
<i> named Victor Zafra,
known by the alias "Tiger."</i>

508
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:31,000
<i>Tiger leads the largest gold
smuggling operations</i>

509
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,400
<i> in the country.</i>

510
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:35,800
<i> His group has abducted miners</i>

511
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:38,733
to force them into illegal work,

512
00:26:38,733 --> 00:26:41,833
<i>and many of them
have lost their lives.</i>

513
00:26:41,833 --> 00:26:44,133
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

514
00:26:44,167 --> 00:26:49,933
<i>Tomorrow, Tiger is scheduled
to meet with Mr. Chan,</i>

515
00:26:49,933 --> 00:26:54,233
<i> a jewelry businessman
in Chinatown.</i>

516
00:26:54,233 --> 00:26:59,500
<i>Your mission, Gabo, is
to bring us Victor Zafra</i>

517
00:26:59,500 --> 00:27:02,067
<i> dead or alive.</i>

518
00:27:02,067 --> 00:27:04,533
<i> If you succeed,</i>

519
00:27:04,533 --> 00:27:08,667
<i> we'll pay you 100,000 pesos.</i>

520
00:27:08,667 --> 00:27:11,500
I have great faith in you, Gabo,

521
00:27:11,500 --> 00:27:15,900
<i> to carry out this mission.</i>

522
00:27:15,933 --> 00:27:19,233
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

523
00:27:19,233 --> 00:27:20,533
[TABLET THUDS]

524
00:27:20,533 --> 00:27:26,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

525
00:27:26,933 --> 00:27:28,067
[GUNSHOTS]

526
00:27:36,267 --> 00:27:37,533
<i> Listen to this, Ricardo.</i>

527
00:27:37,533 --> 00:27:40,267
<i>Your daughter is about
to take down a big syndicate!</i>

528
00:27:40,267 --> 00:27:42,367
<i>Me and your dad are
so proud of you!</i>

529
00:27:43,100 --> 00:27:46,400
<i>Isobel, you're instilling too
much confidence in her.</i>

530
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:47,633
<i> She might get cocky,</i>

531
00:27:47,633 --> 00:27:49,367
<i>when she has yet
to prove herself.</i>

532
00:27:50,433 --> 00:27:51,633
<i>Gabo has learned
about the mission.</i>

533
00:27:51,633 --> 00:27:54,300
The question is, will he do it?

534
00:27:54,300 --> 00:27:56,733
<i> One mission. One job for me.</i>

535
00:27:57,733 --> 00:28:01,633
<i>I have great faith that
he'll take on the mission.</i>

536
00:28:01,633 --> 00:28:02,733
<i> So, what kind of job is it?</i>

537
00:28:02,733 --> 00:28:05,467
<i>Hunting down people
who've broken the law.</i>

538
00:28:05,467 --> 00:28:06,600
<i>(In Cantonese)
May you be prosperous.</i>

539
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:08,233
Mr. Chan, I will see you later.

540
00:28:08,233 --> 00:28:09,433
<i> I have your gold.</i>

541
00:28:09,433 --> 00:28:10,833
<i>So, you're all ready.
Maybe you won't screw it up.</i>

542
00:28:10,833 --> 00:28:12,133
Thanks for the confidence boost.

543
00:28:12,133 --> 00:28:16,467
<i>Thank me once you've
brought in the targets.</i>

544
00:28:16,467 --> 00:28:18,600
If you can actually pull it off.

545
00:28:18,600 --> 00:28:21,567
<i>It's like straight out
of a foreign film!</i>

546
00:28:21,567 --> 00:28:22,933
<i>Like James Bond,
something like that!</i>

547
00:28:22,967 --> 00:28:25,633
- How much are we talking about?
- One hundred thousand pesos.

548
00:28:25,633 --> 00:28:26,800
<i> We'll follow Mr. Chan.</i>

549
00:28:26,800 --> 00:28:29,600
<i> He's going to lead us
to the Tiger.</i>
